2026-10-04T19:12:34.1443649Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-04T19:12:34.1454522Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-04T19:12:34.1455299Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-04T19:12:34.1455792Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-04T19:12:34.1456142Z 
2026-10-04T19:12:34.1456447Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-04T19:12:34.1456883Z 
2026-10-04T19:12:34.1457090Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-04T19:12:34.1457809Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-04T19:12:34.1458051Z 
2026-10-04T19:12:34.1458163Z If you would like to
2026-10-04T19:12:34.1458440Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-04T19:12:34.1458626Z 
2026-10-04T19:12:34.1458817Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-04T19:12:34.1459229Z   $ sh ./install-nix
